[{:db/id "q-127217/selection/4caf0690c6f705bcc5e8636950279e16e39b5e17bf8e3baef1f8414f75ffeba7" :answer/id #uuid "4ef6534d-d0e2-5d4a-828e-6d54a35dd9eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}⟨1,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127217/selection/8a3470c7d49c87a68bdf9cf213b0c22c8691b380bed49d4695e3487baf2e5a27" :answer/id #uuid "09b0dcde-9969-532a-bbec-5af69cadfed3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}⟨{t}^{2},\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127217/selection/109d168654128250626e882017f54be0c757eae5724a0244b313420b207ad4cb" :answer/id #uuid "1931ff5b-c8e4-5c31-a55c-6e58c7f206d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{17}⟨t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127217/selection/7511431af301605865d377a8d041bd746109ee1edaa33a06b83d72cc27514a93" :answer/id #uuid "3ca2c5a4-3614-5489-b00c-e3050b229aa0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{17}⟨1,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127217/selection/0893ba03861d4bde5a2e305c8e9805e44194763e80d24cefa897f8a76ba19fb9" :answer/id #uuid "85f89e65-f49a-53b2-9656-9cccba4e46fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}⟨t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127217/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "24ce1968-c839-52ae-9b07-618a91cb111f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127217/selection/4caf0690c6f705bcc5e8636950279e16e39b5e17bf8e3baef1f8414f75ffeba7" :answer-field/choices ["q-127217/selection/4caf0690c6f705bcc5e8636950279e16e39b5e17bf8e3baef1f8414f75ffeba7" "q-127217/selection/8a3470c7d49c87a68bdf9cf213b0c22c8691b380bed49d4695e3487baf2e5a27" "q-127217/selection/109d168654128250626e882017f54be0c757eae5724a0244b313420b207ad4cb" "q-127217/selection/7511431af301605865d377a8d041bd746109ee1edaa33a06b83d72cc27514a93" "q-127217/selection/0893ba03861d4bde5a2e305c8e9805e44194763e80d24cefa897f8a76ba19fb9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127217" :question/id #uuid "cfd26752-53ee-5373-a6ae-af80bab0a577" :question/math-academy-id "q-127217" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the unit tangent vector to the curve\n $r(t)=⟨2t,\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩$ at an arbitrary point where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )?$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),\\,y(t),\\,z(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $r(t):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(2)}^{2}+(8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}+{(-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+64{cos}^{2}⁡2t+64{sin}^{2}⁡2t} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{1+16({cos}^{2}⁡2t+{sin}^{2}⁡2t)} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{1+16} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{17}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Finally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{17}}⟨2,\\,8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}⟨1,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-127217/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c400d85b-94d5-5fd2-98b4-472ab43c5be4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127217"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-33075"] :question/problem "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j$ at an arbitrary point where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =i+2t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}}(\\,i+2t\\,j)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-74894/selection/0d09b40c1082a8383f4003ec4c17aa07863051ec59fcd7bb9786489ad6182bd3" :answer/id #uuid "60c20d53-4b68-5e10-82a8-e934099d5ace" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2+{t}^{2}}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74894/selection/5df26ca4703dd1840b5e21773d8969c637a3df7b1bd3d6ae1792529e064948bc" :answer/id #uuid "508d59bd-1807-5c3b-98f5-56a466b8455d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4+{t}^{2}}}⟨2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74894/selection/32537f566612817e1b61bc482fa09495a1ad4ae6846966b0d1a5aaee33c3e00b" :answer/id #uuid "1dae1991-b062-50c7-8da4-1be7839a0cd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74894/selection/66634a2875f14bc90279b068921a0f791e07680768dfa25053505350853c0c02" :answer/id #uuid "4ed6d4fc-e6c1-5c98-be42-7ac4a750ca84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4+{t}^{2}}}⟨2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74894/selection/14dfc6cf6528ff135198c69798ab130717a67219578a73963a2251f4f8ac35ae" :answer/id #uuid "d8a6a3fa-18ed-54b0-ba35-6e9b031694a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}}⟨t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74894/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0acab4cb-b32e-5582-b20b-a802ed7c7c5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-74894/selection/66634a2875f14bc90279b068921a0f791e07680768dfa25053505350853c0c02" :answer-field/choices ["q-74894/selection/0d09b40c1082a8383f4003ec4c17aa07863051ec59fcd7bb9786489ad6182bd3" "q-74894/selection/5df26ca4703dd1840b5e21773d8969c637a3df7b1bd3d6ae1792529e064948bc" "q-74894/selection/32537f566612817e1b61bc482fa09495a1ad4ae6846966b0d1a5aaee33c3e00b" "q-74894/selection/66634a2875f14bc90279b068921a0f791e07680768dfa25053505350853c0c02" "q-74894/selection/14dfc6cf6528ff135198c69798ab130717a67219578a73963a2251f4f8ac35ae"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74894" :question/id #uuid "1aa2119a-8b60-5182-b6db-470b5d45c888" :question/math-academy-id "q-74894" :question/problem "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=⟨t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ at an arbitrary point where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),\\,y(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t-2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)+{t}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4+{t}^{2}}}⟨2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-74894/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c400d85b-94d5-5fd2-98b4-472ab43c5be4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74894"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127211/selection/773aaa6e16495d315049aa300a603cb41860ad484ac2a48b0137cc7b20a5a729" :answer/id #uuid "569e869a-3bb7-5e59-ba8c-c89452432287" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4{t}^{2}+25}(t\\,i+2\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127211/selection/e49ea8bd21d4dd4645adacc6ff94d24bad1f508d210c4d44cb13e3ef449d6f11" :answer/id #uuid "7050b782-d189-50db-809f-5b085b4cacff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+5}}(2t\\,i+5\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127211/selection/28851e5753129a39635f663d41c444bc6345f745337f48676de4eb09025f8603" :answer/id #uuid "242fcbb3-dca9-517f-ac13-9519efb776c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+25}}(t\\,i+5{t}^{2}\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127211/selection/d9cb2a19cf9b18e0d36c6a2eee234a243a0b61b6a4e231757d008c3a6d1a7744" :answer/id #uuid "0227e7dd-0ff1-5e36-83c2-128c3706a7ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4{t}^{2}+25}(t\\,i+5\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127211/selection/3b9c64172fe80790eb13730ba062f483143b610f78c24ee7e43e34a03b81e56c" :answer/id #uuid "c5569951-ffb6-5f09-8b46-66f869632392" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+25}}(2t\\,i+5\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127211/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "29e94ec3-bc6e-5179-87fe-e025f639be67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127211/selection/3b9c64172fe80790eb13730ba062f483143b610f78c24ee7e43e34a03b81e56c" :answer-field/choices ["q-127211/selection/773aaa6e16495d315049aa300a603cb41860ad484ac2a48b0137cc7b20a5a729" "q-127211/selection/e49ea8bd21d4dd4645adacc6ff94d24bad1f508d210c4d44cb13e3ef449d6f11" "q-127211/selection/28851e5753129a39635f663d41c444bc6345f745337f48676de4eb09025f8603" "q-127211/selection/d9cb2a19cf9b18e0d36c6a2eee234a243a0b61b6a4e231757d008c3a6d1a7744" "q-127211/selection/3b9c64172fe80790eb13730ba062f483143b610f78c24ee7e43e34a03b81e56c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127211" :question/id #uuid "5fa746e8-ef7f-5a00-9b48-22a2a10656c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-127211" :question/problem "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i+5t\\,j$ at an arbitrary point where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5t)\\,j \\\\  & =2t\\,i+5\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+(5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+25}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+25}}(2t\\,i+5\\,j)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127211/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c400d85b-94d5-5fd2-98b4-472ab43c5be4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127211"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-33063/selection/97dc73c8bc07dc91d5b3ca223c5095360da8644d3ba44065a57159452d4ef21b" :answer/id #uuid "5376295b-5296-5360-80bb-5d5f8c66a884" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,i-\\frac{1}{2}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33063/selection/73aeca2d36dd792b22025f985da5f970953e48be6a99306cbe145f93d78266cc" :answer/id #uuid "8918ebe5-9502-588a-bd62-57f724661f80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,i-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33063/selection/49b3ac5580d63fe44a690b973aaf26fa6bf6481f09191a3997ec52340ff270b3" :answer/id #uuid "3343ce15-2b39-5a59-898f-f05b1fdaeb6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33063/selection/6a172a944ec6afc0e8666cd4022a45f276cdef0faadb4627c04984dd68962dc9" :answer/id #uuid "9f5ce95a-3f4c-5eb9-9490-0ac3522a9694" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,i+\\frac{1}{2}\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33063/selection/a41d9044fc38877b414ec5d67164e1a4a50e6745ee69961c3138fac8d4bcf4c6" :answer/id #uuid "f35917c2-0e8f-5c18-8845-f0681a0bc95e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33063/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "73a1b983-2a14-5bd5-8891-d0695f44a963" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-33063/selection/a41d9044fc38877b414ec5d67164e1a4a50e6745ee69961c3138fac8d4bcf4c6" :answer-field/choices ["q-33063/selection/97dc73c8bc07dc91d5b3ca223c5095360da8644d3ba44065a57159452d4ef21b" "q-33063/selection/73aeca2d36dd792b22025f985da5f970953e48be6a99306cbe145f93d78266cc" "q-33063/selection/49b3ac5580d63fe44a690b973aaf26fa6bf6481f09191a3997ec52340ff270b3" "q-33063/selection/6a172a944ec6afc0e8666cd4022a45f276cdef0faadb4627c04984dd68962dc9" "q-33063/selection/a41d9044fc38877b414ec5d67164e1a4a50e6745ee69961c3138fac8d4bcf4c6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-33063" :question/id #uuid "d602d4dd-c1db-593a-a69d-b6391433b00a" :question/math-academy-id "q-33063" :question/problem "What is the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k$ at the point $P(2\\pi ,1,0)?$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)\\,j+y(t)\\,j+z(t)\\,k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by \n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(2\\pi ,1,0)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =2\\pi \\,i+\\,j+0\\,k \\\\ t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k & =2\\pi \\,i+\\,j+0\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}t=2\\pi  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t=1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t=0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equality, $t=2\\pi .$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, the point $P(2\\pi ,1,0)$ is at the tip of $r(2\\pi ).$  \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=2\\pi :$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k \\\\ {r}^{′}(2\\pi ) & =\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )\\,k \\\\  & =i+0\\,j+\\,k \\\\  & =i+k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(2\\pi ):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(2\\pi )‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+0+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(2\\pi )$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at $P(2\\pi ,1,0):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(2\\pi ) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(2\\pi )}{‖{r}^{′}(2\\pi )‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot (i+k) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-33063/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ff1822c-afad-54f8-aa36-7e0de79d9d04"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-33063"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-33130/selection/59f2d4468a75b2c6603d6c893256974f8654061de835549385351dcd0e285d46" :answer/id #uuid "c163d914-4c41-5823-9018-0b71ad52a136" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}\\,i+\\frac{4}{9}\\,j+\\frac{8}{9}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33130/selection/259417161968af7f0f3de3cec526e741cd1b58c789dcc656fab9f75845f9375a" :answer/id #uuid "ad3c3225-936e-5ddb-8740-1383464fc3d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}\\,i+\\frac{8}{9}\\,j+\\frac{4}{9}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33130/selection/59568adfdcf0e9632eb9992bfbd6c529e88b7a6b3a697c823d59d522b589ea54" :answer/id #uuid "e98b6323-9699-590b-942e-de3e219951b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{21}\\,i+\\frac{2\\sqrt{21}}{21}\\,j+\\frac{4\\sqrt{21}}{21}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33130/selection/f3441a052da04196ff46b5db3390a1b5afef55b39cd3affe0090dd6bf7f7eee3" :answer/id #uuid "93abbcdd-dda5-5be5-9ec0-2ddc58c78c3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{69}}{69}\\,i+\\frac{2\\sqrt{69}}{69}\\,j+\\frac{8\\sqrt{69}}{69}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33130/selection/414517c421891cd13b1683489f9988cdee651f8a5440bcb9574df0e951aa61b8" :answer/id #uuid "cb19ffd7-3b5e-51ac-a670-7cbc18bae9bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\,i+\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33130/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1c0ccf0a-27ac-53db-808d-ef3b6a1afb80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-33130/selection/59f2d4468a75b2c6603d6c893256974f8654061de835549385351dcd0e285d46" :answer-field/choices ["q-33130/selection/59f2d4468a75b2c6603d6c893256974f8654061de835549385351dcd0e285d46" "q-33130/selection/259417161968af7f0f3de3cec526e741cd1b58c789dcc656fab9f75845f9375a" "q-33130/selection/59568adfdcf0e9632eb9992bfbd6c529e88b7a6b3a697c823d59d522b589ea54" "q-33130/selection/f3441a052da04196ff46b5db3390a1b5afef55b39cd3affe0090dd6bf7f7eee3" "q-33130/selection/414517c421891cd13b1683489f9988cdee651f8a5440bcb9574df0e951aa61b8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-33130" :question/id #uuid "a8caefcc-50a5-53a2-a269-288ed0a3e61d" :question/math-academy-id "q-33130" :question/problem "What is the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+2{t}^{2}\\,k$ at the point $P(2,4,8)?$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)\\,j+y(t)\\,j+z(t)\\,k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(2,4,8)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =2\\,i+4\\,j+8\\,k \\\\ t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+2{t}^{2}\\,k & =2\\,i+4\\,j+8\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}t=2 \\\\ {t}^{2}=4 \\\\ 2{t}^{2}=8.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equality, $t=2.$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, the point $P(2,4,8)$ is at the tip of $r(2).$ \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =i+2t\\,j+4t\\,k \\\\ {r}^{′}(2) & =\\,i+2\\cdot 2\\,j+4\\cdot 2\\,k \\\\  & =i+4\\,j+8\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(2)‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{81} \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(2)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at $P(2,4,8):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(2) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(2)}{‖{r}^{′}(2)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot (i+4\\,j+8\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\,i+\\frac{4}{9}\\,j+\\frac{8}{9}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-33130/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ff1822c-afad-54f8-aa36-7e0de79d9d04"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-33130"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-75228/selection/b01ad7edbfe792b7ec03208695ec18e20e30d350b0b9ec3e73b1ce7b855cb417" :answer/id #uuid "d30f135f-7a76-5047-8108-8f0ae2113c17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}(-2\\,i+\\,j+2\\,k)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75228/selection/e651539f34631d88238d70fced7de4ff8697b63f9ca8e69c6c2a10116a3fdf52" :answer/id #uuid "7c24304d-0dfa-5f28-b057-ef4898866955" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\,i+\\,j+2\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75228/selection/55fedcd5e13e277595c9856384bf33ed169bf84ec469b0de9447b2a6ce91b354" :answer/id #uuid "2d7eb5b0-3b23-50f0-bd08-4b328cc3726e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{9}\\,i+\\frac{1}{9}\\,j+\\frac{2}{9}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75228/selection/30878150f91a56604b184ba3dd33ca894f44443098ec1c51c7eaa2a60e753533" :answer/id #uuid "8ff5b82c-6a31-5bea-8e21-b94c774ee623" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}(2\\,i-\\,j-2\\,k)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75228/selection/e8867e75ce59ed3da173334db58e702b4fb5be8f4113af6f46571dc4ae07addc" :answer/id #uuid "c20a9918-d679-53b5-be45-663273d3009f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{1}{3}\\,j+\\frac{2}{3}\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75228/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0969ac4b-bcfa-5c68-8c78-e3e4deff1649" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75228/selection/e8867e75ce59ed3da173334db58e702b4fb5be8f4113af6f46571dc4ae07addc" :answer-field/choices ["q-75228/selection/b01ad7edbfe792b7ec03208695ec18e20e30d350b0b9ec3e73b1ce7b855cb417" "q-75228/selection/e651539f34631d88238d70fced7de4ff8697b63f9ca8e69c6c2a10116a3fdf52" "q-75228/selection/55fedcd5e13e277595c9856384bf33ed169bf84ec469b0de9447b2a6ce91b354" "q-75228/selection/30878150f91a56604b184ba3dd33ca894f44443098ec1c51c7eaa2a60e753533" "q-75228/selection/e8867e75ce59ed3da173334db58e702b4fb5be8f4113af6f46571dc4ae07addc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75228" :question/id #uuid "0205390e-d98e-5033-a317-b12907a8ca1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-75228" :question/problem "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=({t}^{2}-2t)p(t)$ at the point corresponding to $t=1$, given that  $p(1)=i+2\\,j-k\\,$ and $\\,{p}^{′}(1)=2\\,i-\\,j-2\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j+z(t)k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(({t}^{2}-2t)p(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2t)\\cdot p(t)+({t}^{2}-2t)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(p(t)) \\\\  & =(2t-2)\\,p(t)+({t}^{2}-2t)\\,{p}^{′}(t) \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =(2(1)-2)\\,p(1)+((1)^{2}-2(1))\\,{p}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =0-{p}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =-(2\\,i-\\,j-2\\,k) \\\\  & =-2i+\\,j+2k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖r(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(1)^{2}+(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(1)}{‖{r}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-2\\,i+j+2k) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{1}{3}\\,j+\\frac{2}{3}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector to the curve at the point that corresponds to $t=1$ is  $T(1)=-\\frac{2}{3}\\,i+\\frac{1}{3}\\,j+\\frac{2}{3}\\,k.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-75228/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "34342124-8cee-5b70-bf57-64f746af8912"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75228"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-64486"] :question/problem "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,p(t)$ at the point corresponding to $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$, given that  $p(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\,i-\\,j+2k\\,$ and $\\,{p}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\,i+\\,j.$" :question/worked-solution "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j+z(t)k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,p(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot p(t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(p(t)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,p(t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{p}^{′}(t) \\\\ {r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})p(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}){p}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(i-\\,j+2k)+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(i+\\,j) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}(i+k)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})‖ & =\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}+(0)^{2}+(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}{‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}(i+k) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(i+k)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector to the curve at the point that corresponds to $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is\n $T(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(i+k).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3054"] :question/problem "What is the unit tangent vector to the curve ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/assets/1a5a0925f4e15e00c9eff4bb4f39ce9c6eda232881bbddb07184ac54bbc269a8.png) at the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14079396/assets/1e24125540d8b43cf8d314684fef6fb5be15c62d6988f9aac984f9812e6a74fd.png)" 